From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: IvyCZE <me@ivy.yt>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 19:30:47 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Embermine: 0004-privacy-defaults

Ship with telemetry and crash reporting off: BuildConfig TELEMETRY and CRASH_REPORTING default to false, the usage, daily usage ping, experimentation, crash report and sponsored/Pocket defaults are off. Crashes stay in the local crash list, and Socorro is registered only after the user picks Ask or Auto in Data collection (Sentry still needs CRASH_REPORTING). The Data collection page shows the marketing data and crash report sections in every build. Nimbus experiment fetches run only after the user opts in to experimentation. The Glean collection switch follows the stored choice at launch and changes as soon as the user toggles it.

Gecko's own telemetry upload and region lookup default to off through GeckoPreferenceController on the default branch, applied as soon as the runtime is created. Embermine ships Mozilla's prebuilt GeckoView, so a change to the bundled default pref file would never reach the APK.

Safe Browsing is disabled unless the optional SAFE_BROWSING_API_KEY is provided at build time (read from the git-ignored .safe_browsing_api_key file into BuildConfig). With a key, the Google legacy, v4 and v5 GeckoView providers use it; without one, no provider is configured and the Safe Browsing policy is NONE.

The onboarding Terms of Use line says Embermine does not send diagnostic or interaction data to Mozilla unless turned on, in every locale. Onboarding no longer submits the onboarding-opt-out ping when telemetry is off: that ping does not follow the collection setting, so it reached incoming.telemetry.mozilla.org on every fresh install.

Co-authored-by: factory-droid[bot] <138933559+factory-droid[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>

